  "local_modifications": [
    "Stages 1 and 2 consume versioned prepared data bundles and normalized seeds without native runtime imports.",
    "Adaptive n-gram sampling, weighted clustering, empirical length sampling and frozen-center recovery retained.",
    "Stage 3 retains sequence-conditioned candidate/fixture generation, whole-action partial hints, patching and regeneration.",
    "Benchmark-specific implementations and resources removed from the maintained TASTE subset.",
    "EA task service supplies checks, assertion synthesis, alignment, native execution/grading and export through validate/export.",
    "Generic candidate task payload plus normalized reference_actions replace native task-field access in generation.",
    "Prepared data/prompt fingerprints, length distributions and generation settings bind checkpoints, recovery and resume.",
    "Generated task records retain candidate, fixture and native task separately from private validation and hint evidence.",
    "Original license retained; independent EA native integrations reside outside the vendor tree.",
    "Unused evolution sources excluded; formatting/import cleanup applied to the maintained subset.",
    "Sequence-only recovery selection is shared by the automated runner and the skill-led Stage 3 helper; native interactions can run outside TASTE.",
    "Stage 1/2 append-only private journals retain every seed/draw, validator transport response/usage, replacement and recovery round without changing sequence algorithms.",
    "Stage 1 recovery verifies and replays linked immutable decision journals, preserves pending draws, records explicit legacy RNG resets, and saves complete Python/NumPy random state for later continuation."
  ]
